// `std.authority`: the ambient authority. `std` reaches the host by
// capability, on `cap-std`'s design. Authority enters a program in one place,
// as `main`'s parameter, `def main(authority : Authority)`, and never through
// a global. That is what `cap_std::ambient_authority()` marks in Rust, and
// `gandr run` hands it to `main` once.
//
// Each host module opens its root capability from it by attenuation. A
// capability holding more operations stands where a program asks for one
// holding fewer. A holder never reaches an operation its own capability does
// not hold. The authority holds the operations of every landed host module of
// the map, and grows as each one lands.
//
// - see: `../README.md` — the map of host modules

/// The ambient authority: every host operation a landed module of `std`
/// reaches, held once, as `main`'s parameter.
pub type Authority = Cap { print, eprint, read_line };

/// The standard streams' root capability, opened from `authority`.
pub def console(authority : Authority) -> Cap { print, eprint, read_line } {
  authority
}
